ear Purgatoire R near Las Animas affecting Bent\nCounty.\n\nFor the Purgatoire River...including Purgatoire near Las Animas...\nMinor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Purgatoire River near Purgatoire R near Las Animas.\n\n* WHEN...From this morning to Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor Flood. Minor agricultural flooding\noccurs into low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:15 AM MDT Thursday the stage was 8.9 feet.\n- Forecast...The river will rise above flood stage late this\nmorning to 10.5 feet this evening. It will then fall early\ntomorrow afternoon. It will rise to 9.5 feet Saturday morning. It\nwill then fall below flood stage late Saturday evening.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 10.5\nfeet on 08/19/2004.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-04T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Bent, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3e98b8d6f90a246f1361b950c20f3b9588e9d2a7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3e98b8d6f90a246f1361b950c20f3b9588e9d2a7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 1 at 8:42AM MDT until October 1 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The Southeast Mountains and the southeast plains.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon MDT today.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of heavy rainfall associated with a remnant tropical\nstorm system will spread across southern Colorado through\nThursday.\n\n- The Southeast Mountains, including the Aspen Acres burn area, and\nthe southeast plains.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-01T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northern Sangre de 